    "reasoning": "All 17 selected field values agree with their own captured worked solutions. Two source qualifications remain: q-82338 incorrectly writes y-2 as the lower x-bound in its intermediate type II region; the correct bound is y+2, which its final integral correctly uses. q-17552 gives the valid nonzero solution family but omits the equilibrium solution y=0; y=1 is included by C=0. Mathematical checks: q-126031 integrates (1+x)^(-2) from 2 to infinity to obtain 1/3. q-337570 has original slope -y/x, so orthogonal slope x/y gives y^2=x^2+K. q-17552 substitutes z=1/y to obtain z'-z=-1 and hence y=1/(1+Ce^x). q-343302 uses Abel's identity W'=-W/(x^2+1), giving W=Ce^(-arctan(x)); W(0)=2 makes W positive everywhere. q-98525 factors y^2+y-2=(y-1)(y+2), giving upward arrows below -2 and above 1 and a downward arrow between them, as in option 0. q-163548 integrates v dv/dx=4-x to obtain v^2=52-(x-4)^2, whose maximum positive velocity is 2 sqrt(13). q-335282 gives X=3-1.5e^(-0.4t), so reaching 2 L takes 2.5 ln(3/2), approximately 1.014 minutes, rounding to 1. q-118552 has carrying capacity 1.2/0.002=600, approached asymptotically from the initial population 100. q-86676 computes G=P diag(-1,2) P^(-1); the resulting matrix maps (3,5) to (-3,-5) and (1,2) to (2,4). q-81190 has eigenvalues plus and minus 3i, with component ratios 5/(1+3i) and 5/(1-3i); their product is 25/10=5/2, independent of eigenvector scaling. q-82338 reverses the region to 0<=y<=2 and y+2<=x<=4. q-105895 applies curl(fF)=f curl(F)+grad(f) cross F to obtain (0,-1,2). q-163642 evaluates the Hessian as [[4,-2],[-2,-6]], with determinant -24-4=-28. q-80778 uses the equivalent level surface 3z^2+2xy=1, whose normal at the point is proportional to (-2,2,6), giving c/b=3. q-32522 computes (1,1,-1) cross (4,0,2)=(2,-6,-4). No final selected answer disagrees with MA; the source errors concern intermediate wording and completeness.",
